List the settings a browser can actually reach

Ten Settings sections were missing from the tile that the desktop shows: Orca
Account, Mobile, Plugins, SSH Hosts, Browser, Computer Use, Voice, Notifications,
Advanced and Mobile Emulator. Settings search could not find them either, so
there was no route to any of them.

One line decided all of it - `showDesktopOnlySettings = !isWebClient` - and it
conflated three different questions: does this need a desktop CLIENT, does it
need a particular HOST, and has anyone wired it yet. Only the first is about the
browser, and this repository exists because the browser must not lose what the
desktop has.

Each site now asks its own question. Orca Account, Mobile, Plugins, SSH Hosts,
Browser and Computer Use are listed: their RPC families are registered and
reachable from the tile today, and `browser.screencast.v1` is advertised by
`orca serve` on the artifact (read off `status.get`, which also settles
Contradictions #4 in `docs/audit/v1.4.190/99-cross-cutting.md`). Computer Use
answers `computer.capabilities` with what the host is missing - on Linux, the
python3-gi and AT-SPI packages - and hiding the section hid that answer.

Mobile Emulator and macOS Permissions move onto the host axis. Both were gated on
`isMac`, which is `isMacUserAgent()` - the machine RENDERING, not the machine the
runtime runs on. `status.get` reports `hostPlatform`, and the nav hook already
resolves it, so a browser driving a Mac host now sees them and a Mac driving a
Linux host no longer does. That second case was wrong before any browser was
involved.

Three stay hidden, with the reason recorded at each: Notifications configures
NATIVE desktop toasts through `RuntimeDesktopSurface`, which is inert with no
renderer and whose work the runtime already routes to paired clients instead;
Advanced writes `httpProxyUrl`, absent from the `SettingsUpdate` schema and held
as a protected secret, so a web client's edits would be silently discarded; Voice
has eight registered `speech.*` methods but no `speech` namespace in
`web-preload-api.ts` at all, so its pane would be entirely dead controls - the
design that closes it is `docs/audit/v1.4.190/N2-speech-design.md`. The system
tray and menu bar rows are correct as they stand: a browser tab has neither.

Warp import is on the wrong axis too - it reads the HOST's Warp config - but
`AppearancePane.tsx` makes the same call independently, so it is left alone
rather than half-moved.

Two patches in this series were dead behind this and are now reachable, which is
why their own `To test` lines were unfollowable: `plugins-web-bridge.diff` says
to open Settings > Plugins in the tile, and `pairing-credentials.diff` says to
open Settings > Mobile. Both headers are corrected in this commit.

To test, open Settings in the tile: Orca Account, Mobile, Plugins, SSH Hosts,
Browser and Computer Use should be listed, and searching for "plugin" should find
them. Covered by `settings-nav-web-parity.test.ts`, which asserts the web nav
both ways - what it must list, and what must stay hidden - and pins that desktop
behaviour is unchanged.
